{"seq":1,"slug":"knowing-and-ignorance","title":"Knowing And Ignorance","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/ideas-and-methods/knowing-and-ignorance","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"i-know-that-i-know-nothing","title":"自知无知","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/ideas-and-methods/knowing-and-ignorance/i-know-that-i-know-nothing","wordCount":1599,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"knowledge-is-virtue","title":"美德即知识","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/ideas-and-methods/knowing-and-ignorance/knowledge-is-virtue","wordCount":1692,"readingTime":7}],"introMarkdown":"本章呈现苏格拉底关于知识的两个核心思想。\"自知无知\"——承认并认识到自己的无知，是智慧的起点与求知的开端；\"美德即知识\"——德性的本质在于知识，作恶源于无知。这两个深刻而富有争议的命题，将认识与道德紧密联系，构成了苏格拉底思想中关于知与无知、知与行的核心洞见。\n"}